Z||000003||Raydar||06-29-2000||09:41 AM||||86... If your car still has the rubber water seal at the front edge of the decklid, remove it before you have the recall work done. If you don't, it will disappear as part of the recall.<BR>I don't have a clue as to why. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Majik||06-29-2000||02:14 PM||||If the recall has not been done on your car, they have to comply with it no matter the age/milage/condition of the vehicle.<BR>I just had a recall done on my 86 for free, just went in there with the full recall information in hand (found on Michagan's Fiero Page)...and 3 days later (after ordering parts) it was done...cost?  $0!  <P>Good luck on it!||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||06-29-2000||02:40 PM||||Back in '97 before I got the car It was looked over to see if anything was wrong with it.  They said a cracked manifold would cost $550 to fix!!!!  Luckily I found out the recall work was not done on it......<P>Alright, I'll take the water seal off.  I think they were afraid of that ralling on the manifold.......but im not sure.||||reg||10
