Z||000009||86SE||06-29-2000||04:35 PM||||I called one Pontiac dealer and told them about the recall, they said "We dont do that work anymore, its too old" i say "even if it envolves the saftey of the passengers?", he "Nope".    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Called another one, gave them my VIN, he called back 10 min later, "I ran the VIN trhough and it dident come up with any recalls"........WTF is goin on??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by 86SE (edited 06-29-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000010||87ECO5||06-29-2000||04:50 PM||||Not sure how true this is ...<P>I heard the reason they remove(d) the "rain gutter" strip from the front of the decklid is (was) because the engineers decided that removing it would aid in the cooling of the engine bay.<P>Who knows ...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ed||06-29-2000||06:47 PM||||Yes, the drip strip was removed to allow for better cooling.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Majik||06-30-2000||12:53 PM||||The recall information will be under the deck lid.  You should have 2 or 3 stickers (depending on the year/style of the car).<P>Recall information can be found here: <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/MI_Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/MI_Fiero.htm</A> <BR>near the bottom of the page (thank you Michagan Fiero Club!!!).<P>As for my recall work, I even called Pontiac in Michagan, and they confirmed that they did indeed have to fulfill the recall work.  If you read on the recall for the brakes, it states (in GM's own print) that the recall work must be done ... here...in their own words:  "Dealers are to service all vehicles subject to this campaign at no charge to owners, regardless of mileage, age of vehicle, or ownership, from this time forward."<P>Print the recalls out (what I did) and hand it to the service manager (what I did) and they should have no questions on if they will do it or not.<P>Hope this helps...and good luck to you on getting the work done.   Any questions, feel free to E-mail me.<P>Majik||||reg||1
Z||000013||86SE||07-01-2000||06:29 PM||||I called the Pontiac Service Shop again and no recalls were still outstanding.<P>I know back in about 1993 the Fiero was wrecked in New York with 55,000 miles on it.  What I think what happen was, the Fiero was hit from behind, smashing the decklid, bumper, tail lights, and notchback clip piece (over $1K in dammage supposidly).  Im pretty sure it was hit from behind because the left side tail lights dont quite line up, and the deklid is uneven at the points where it closes (by the left side tail light).<P>So, when the fixed it, they probibly put a new decklid on (any recall sitckers would not be replaced).  The front side manifold looks fairly "new", it looks nothing like the rear manifold.  The front one has no rust on it like the rear one.  There is also a heat sheild covering most of the frnt manifold.<P>Does anybody have pictures of an engine compartment after the recall work as been done??||||reg||5
Z||000014||Majik||07-02-2000||04:47 PM||||I'll try to do that this week for you, since I have just had the work done.  anything in particular you want to see?  rear heat sheiding, front manifold, my dog?  let me know, either by email or in here...I'll get 'em for you.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>Majik||||reg||1
